{"pageid":4864,"title":"Rock Candy","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Rock Candy</span>","revid":21009,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Rock Candy</b> is a holiday rock that spawns during the <b>2025 Christmas Event</b>, inside <a href=\"/wiki/Mike%27s_Mines\" title=\"Mike&#39;s Mines\">Mike's Mines</a> and near the <a href=\"/wiki/Lost_Woods\" title=\"Lost Woods\">Lost Woods</a><sup>1</sup>.\nAs they are a seasonal rock, they may be sold for the seasonal currency, <b>Snowflakes (❄️)</b>. They <b>do not</b> sell for cash.\n</p><p>The Rock Candy appears in two variants: <b>Purple Rock Candy</b> and <b>Yellow Rock Candy</b>. The variants are identical in functionality, with the latter being slightly more expensive.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/e/e0/Rock_Candy_Transparency.png/revision/latest?cb=20251226093147\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"An image of Lightslate placed behind three chunks of Yellow Rock Candy. Raw (Left), Refined (Middle), and Forged (Right).\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Rock Candy Transparency.png\" data-image-key=\"Rock_Candy_Transparency.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/e/e0/Rock_Candy_Transparency.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20251226093147\" /></a> \t<noscript><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/e/e0/Rock_Candy_Transparency.png/revision/latest?cb=20251226093147\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"An image of Lightslate placed behind three chunks of Yellow Rock Candy. Raw (Left), Refined (Middle), and Forged (Right).\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/e/e0/Rock_Candy_Transparency.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20251226093147\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Rock Candy Transparency.png\" data-image-key=\"Rock_Candy_Transparency.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/e/e0/Rock_Candy_Transparency.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20251226093147\" /></a></noscript> \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Rock_Candy_Transparency.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">Lightslate placed behind Rock Candy to demonstrate transparency</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure><p>Rock Candy is also <b>transparent in all forms</b>, with the transparency decreasing as the rock is processed. It is the most transparent when Raw, and the least transparent when Forged. This transparency also carries over to blueprints.\n</p><div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<p>Unlike other nodes, Rock Candy may also form in a tall cluster of interlocking cubes, rather than a standard cluster, making it easier to spot in darkness.\n</p><p>Rock Candy is currently <b>unobtainable</b> naturally, and may only be obtained by trading with another player, or, another Christmas event occurs, re-adding Rock Candy nodes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Variants\">Variants</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Yellow_Rock_Candy\">Yellow Rock Candy</span></h3>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-wikia pi-layout-default type-wood\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"title\">Rock Candy</h2>\n\n\t<div class=\"pi-image-collection wds-tabber\